# Raw session masters (the multi-hundred-MB .wav files) stay out of git —
# committing those would push ~2 GB into history permanently.
#
# The compressed .mp3 recordings are the exception, and they live in audio/.
# They have to be repo files rather than release assets: GitHub serves release
# downloads as application/octet-stream with Content-Disposition: attachment,
# which WebKit refuses to play (MediaError.code 4), so the timecode links were
# dead on every iPhone at the table. Pages serves the same bytes as audio/mp3
# with byte ranges honoured, which plays and seeks.
*.mp3
!audio/*.mp3
*.wav
*.m4a
*.aac
*.flac
*.ogg
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv

# Local scratch
*.tmp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
